course: dictionary
lesson: 14216
title: Murdered: the serious meaning and the slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Murdered» is the past form of the verb «murder». It means a person was killed on purpose by someone else. This is the most serious crime there is, so the word is used about real terrible events in stories, history and the news.
explain: Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The detective found out who had murdered the old man in the book.» The detective, the crime and the investigation show that the serious meaning is the right one.
explain: Some people use the word as a joke or to exaggerate. «She murdered that song on stage» means she sang it very badly, and nobody was hurt. «We got murdered 7–0 in the match» means we lost very badly. Look at the clues before you decide what the word means.
explain: Real danger is never a joke. If you ever see or hear about someone being hurt or in danger, tell a grown-up straight away and phone the police.
fact: «Murdered» means killed on purpose by another person.
fact: Murder is the most serious crime, so it appears in stories, detective books and history lessons.
fact: Informally, «murdered» can mean done very badly: «She murdered that song» means she sang it terribly.
fact: In sport slang, «we got murdered» means we lost very badly. «I could murder a cup of tea» means I want one very much.
fact: Real violence must always be reported to the police, and you should tell a grown-up you trust.
exercise: «The detective found out who had murdered the old man in the story.» What does murdered mean here? | Wanted something very much | Sang very badly | Lost a game very badly | *Killed someone on purpose
exercise: «She murdered that song on stage, and her friends covered their ears.» What does murdered mean here? | *Sang it very badly | Sang it very quietly | Wrote a brand new song | Killed the singer
exercise: «I could murder a cup of tea after that long walk.» What does it mean? | I dropped the tea on the floor | Someone wants to hurt a person | *I want a cup of tea very much | I need to cook a meal
test: «We got murdered 7–0 in the match.» What does murdered mean in this sentence? | *We lost very badly | We played a very good game | We scored seven goals
test: In a detective story, what does it mean if a character was murdered? | They were lost in a forest | *Someone killed them on purpose | They sang the wrong song | They were very tired after a long day
exam: If you ever see someone being really hurt, what should you do? | Ignore it and carry on walking | Wait and see if it stops | Post a joke about it online | *Tell a grown-up straight away and phone the police
